A $1,000 share position with no real money attached, and it enters at the next session's

00:03:07.623 --> 00:03:12.223
open under the published rules and is judged against the NASDAQ over its own five sessions.

00:03:12.223 --> 00:03:18.363
The Motley Fool Canada reports third-quarter property revenue rose 6.7% year-over-year

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:27.003
to $161.3 million Canadian dollars with net operating income or NOI up 8.5% supported

00:03:27.003 --> 00:03:29.063
by existing properties and acquisitions.

00:03:29.503 --> 00:03:36.043
The units trade at $18 Canadian dollars and 45 cents with a 5.3% annualized yield and

00:03:36.043 --> 00:03:42.023
99.5% occupancy, price sitting above recent lows with volume supporting the distribution

00:03:42.023 --> 00:03:47.883
and the trust owns over 380 commercial properties covering nearly 32 million square feet.

00:03:48.303 --> 00:03:55.263
Canadian tire its largest tenant. A 5% stop loss caps the simulated loss at $50 on the $1,000

00:03:55.263 --> 00:04:02.023
position, if occupancy or rental trends deteriorate. The invalidation is portfolio occupancy reported

00:04:02.023 --> 00:04:08.903
below 99% in the next available update, and the target is plus 2% to plus 4% over the five

00:04:08.903 --> 00:04:11.983
session window if monthly payouts stability holds.

00:04:12.503 --> 00:04:16.143
Confidence is medium, yield support, and the occupancy print align.

00:04:16.703 --> 00:04:22.063
Yet sector rotation pressure on real estate investment trusts or REITs remains the uncertainty,

00:04:22.543 --> 00:04:26.743
which is the same medium grade the last closed hold carried when the setup was mixed.

00:04:28.121 --> 00:04:32.321
Occupancy is the early warning layer here, the way the polymarket contract was the early

00:04:32.321 --> 00:04:37.261
warning layer on leadership risk, and the screen follows valuation discipline by filtering

00:04:37.261 --> 00:04:41.461
monthly payers on occupancy and revenue growth rather than headline yield alone.

00:04:42.041 --> 00:04:47.201
The same valuation discipline that tagged the rail hold, plus dividend compounding inside

00:04:47.201 --> 00:04:51.001
a TFSA where monthly cash can reinvest without a tax drag.

