The full history since March 2026 covers 102 trades with a 53% win rate and cumulative

00:09:02.423 --> 00:09:09.963
simulated profit of $75.79, and every number is reproducible from the pick. The next session

00:09:09.963 --> 00:09:16.773
open, the name stop, and the fifth session close. No discretionary exits. You hold a rate-sensitive

00:09:16.773 --> 00:09:24.153
name like BMO in your TFSA, and the stock drops 0.42% after a quiet session, while the broader

00:09:24.153 --> 00:09:32.893
TSX is already under pressure. Do you treat that print as a symmetric hawkish signal, or do you

00:09:32.893 --> 00:09:36.513
in comments circulating on X, made the asymmetry explicit.

00:09:37.133 --> 00:09:39.073
Labor market repairs take far longer

00:09:39.073 --> 00:09:40.253
than inflation adjustments,

00:09:40.733 --> 00:09:43.133
so the committee can cut the policy rate gradually

00:09:43.133 --> 00:09:45.413
over several meetings when labor weakens,

00:09:45.793 --> 00:09:48.093
while inflation still demands faster action.

00:09:48.813 --> 00:09:52.393
The mechanism is not, the Fed always balances both sides equally.

00:09:52.973 --> 00:09:55.493
It is a documented preference for gradual easing

00:09:55.493 --> 00:09:58.153
on the labor side because shortfalls are hard to reverse,

00:09:58.693 --> 00:10:00.913
which is also why Bank of Canada decisions

00:10:00.913 --> 00:10:04.033
often track the same labor versus inflation trade-off.

00:10:04.353 --> 00:10:09.313
The habit is to map each official's prior language on repair speed before you touch duration

00:10:09.313 --> 00:10:16.933
or sector exposure in a TFA or a registered retirement savings plan, or RRSP, instead of

00:10:16.933 --> 00:10:19.533
treating every central bank sentence as a coin flip.

00:10:20.093 --> 00:10:22.513
The misconception is that every signal is balanced.

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:28.033
The fix is to score the speaker's labor versus inflation waiting first, then decide whether

00:10:28.033 --> 00:10:33.548
the rate-sensitive name still belongs at the same size. Open your broker-jap, locate

00:10:33.548 --> 00:10:38.968
any REIT or monthly pair holding, and calculate its current annualized yield using the most

00:10:38.968 --> 00:10:44.208
recent distribution amount divided by today's price. Occupancy and revenue growth still

00:10:44.208 --> 00:10:50.388
sit above that headline number. Before we wrap, CRT.UN starts its five-session clock at the

00:10:50.388 --> 00:10:55.448
next session's open, and the occupancy filter is the line that kills the thesis if it breaks.

